{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs1KA1JSZbRxkAt6fDvV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`resolver/solve.py` is implemented, and all 9 tests in `tests/test_resolver.py` pass.\n\n- **Version and Constraint:** `Version` compares numerically component by component, so `1.0 == 1` and `1.10 > 1.9`. `Constraint.parse` handles all six operators and comma-separated lists, with `.name` and `.allows(Version)`.\n- **Search:** `resolve` backtracks over the packages in alphabetical order and tries versions from highest to lowest. It checks each choice against its dependencies right away and prunes versions that can never be satisfied. Cycles are handled.\n- **Errors:** an unsatisfiable request raises `ResolutionError` naming the package where the search dead-ended, for example `b` when `a` needs `b<1`. A root package missing from the index is named too.\n- **Preference rule:** the solution is lexicographically greatest by package name only when the set of required packages is the same across solutions. If a different version choice would pull in an alphabetically earlier package, the order isn't well defined, and the resolver doesn't try to resolve that case.\n- **Tests:** they cover the spec example, cycles, backtracking, unreachable packages, error naming, and a 40-package chain that runs instantly. I did not test an index with a few hundred versions like the hidden one. My first version of the large test hung until I added the pruning."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14024,"cache_read_input_tokens":53659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14024},"output_tokens":451,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67aade60-775e-4aa5-b26e-46b226fb